### `Close-while-reading aborts process (FORTIFY destroyed mutex)`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| SIGABRT `pthread_mutex_lock called on a destroyed mutex` in `sys_arch_mbox_fetch` via `zts_bsd_read`; whole app dies, proxy port goes dead → `ERR_PROXY_CONNECTION_FAILED` | One thread closes a `ZeroTierSocket` while another thread is blocked in `zts_bsd_read`/`write` on the same fd — `zts_bsd_close` frees the lwip netconn and destroys its mbox mutexes | In duplex relays, **half-close only**: `shutdownOutput()` when a pump finishes; `close()` only after both pump threads joined. Never `close()` a ZT socket another thread may still be reading |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Short zts_bsd_write silently drops bytes`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Large uploads through ZT socket corrupt/truncate; small requests fine | `zts_bsd_write_offset` can return a short count (send buffer full); stock `ZeroTierOutputStream.write` ignores the return value | Loop on the return value until all bytes written (patched in-tree `ZeroTierOutputStream.write`; rebuild AAR per `libzt patch not in APK`) |

